# Architecture Tracking

This project uses `{{architectureFile}}` as a living architecture document. archlearn MCP server is available.

## Rules

1. **On session start**: Read `{{architectureFile}}` first — it is your cross-session memory.
2. **Before major changes**: Re-read `{{architectureFile}}` to align changes with existing architecture.
3. **After major changes**: Update via MCP tools (`update_architecture`, `record_decision`) or edit `{{architectureFile}}` directly.

## Major Changes

Adding/removing services · changing protocols · new frameworks · infrastructure changes · module boundary refactors.

## Requirements

- Every decision MUST include at least one rejected alternative with `whyNot`.
- Every connection MUST reference existing service IDs.
- Always update `project.lastUpdated` and append to `history`.
- Use `npx archlearn reconcile` to detect drift.
